# REQUIRES: python-api
# The derivative of the energy in the charges together with the other
# tunables of one program (D230, #256, docs/python-gradient.md) on the CPU,
# in double and mixed precision: the charges free with PME and tied by a
# map under a Coulomb cutoff, with constants of a pair term and with every
# other kind of tunable at once (the table by pairs and per type, the
# parameters of a term over tuples, an external term that reads the
# charges, an observed constant). Each derivative against central
# differences of the energy that it is the derivative of, and against the
# program that declares the charges alone or the others alone; and what the
# Python model cannot declare beside the charges.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_mixed.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide refusals | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REFUSED
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_mixed.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide test CPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable_mixed.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide test CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# REFUSED: refusals: a constant of an external term: the tunable 'e0': no pair or tuple term is named 'field'
# REFUSED: refusals: a pair term that reads the charges: term 'soft': undeclared parameter 'q1'
# REFUSED: refusals passed
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: PME, charges free, constants a, l of the pair term a exp(-r/l): central differences q
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: cutoff, charges tied (25 entries), constants a, l of the pair term a exp(-r/l): central differences q
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: PME, charges free, all of these at once: central differences q
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: cutoff, charges tied (25 entries), all of these at once: central differences q
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 4 combinations
# CHECK: test passed
